\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The finite levels match}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{The weight #{\bigl(\frac{5}{3}\bigr)^n} multiplies, once at
each refinement, by the reciprocal of the factor
#{\frac{3}{5}} in \ref{fdip-00DS}. For #{m\ge n},
\ref{fdip-00DT} equates the [kept form](fdip-00DF) of level
#{m}, read on #{V_n}, with the energy of level #{n}. Both
sides are quadratic forms on the finite set #{V_n}.
When the weight in \ref{fdip-00DS} is a positive rational,
the determinant displayed there is a nonzero rational.}
